            <div class="lesson-content">
                <h1 class="display-4 mb-3">Methods Basics</h1>
                <div class="d-flex gap-3 mb-4">
                    <span class="badge bg-warning text-dark">Intermediate</span>
                    <span class="badge bg-info text-dark">25 min read</span>
                    <span class="badge bg-primary">Lesson 10 of 13</span>
                </div>

                <h2>What are Methods?</h2>
                <p>Methods are blocks of code that perform specific tasks. They help organize, reuse, and maintain code.</p>

                <h2>Basic Method Structure</h2>
                <pre><code>// Syntax:
[access_modifier] [static] return_type MethodName(parameters)
{
    // Method body
    return value; // if return type is not void
}</code></pre>

                <h2>Method Examples</h2>

                <h3>Void Method (No Return)</h3>
                <pre><code>public void Greet(string name)
{
    Console.WriteLine($"Hello, {name}!");
}

Greet("John"); // Output: Hello, John!</code></pre>

                <h3>Method with Return Value</h3>
                <pre><code>public int Add(int a, int b)
{
    return a + b;
}

int result = Add(5, 3); // result = 8</code></pre>

                <h3>Static Method</h3>
                <pre><code>public static double CalculateCircleArea(double radius)
{
    return Math.PI * radius * radius;
}

double area = CalculateCircleArea(5);</code></pre>

                <h2>Method Parameters</h2>

                <h3>Optional Parameters</h3>
                <pre><code>public void Greet(string name, string greeting = "Hello")
{
    Console.WriteLine($"{greeting}, {name}!");
}

Greet("John");          // Hello, John!
Greet("Jane", "Hi");    // Hi, Jane!</code></pre>

                <h3>Params Array</h3>
                <pre><code>public int Sum(params int[] numbers)
{
    int total = 0;
    foreach (int num in numbers)
        total += num;
    return total;
}

int result = Sum(1, 2, 3, 4, 5); // result = 15</code></pre>

                <h3>Ref and Out Parameters</h3>
                <pre><code>// ref - passes by reference
public void Increment(ref int number)
{
    number++;
}

int x = 5;
Increment(ref x); // x is now 6

// out - returns multiple values
public bool TryDivide(int a, int b, out int result)
{
    if (b == 0)
    {
        result = 0;
        return false;
    }
    result = a / b;
    return true;
}

if (TryDivide(10, 2, out int quotient))
{
    Console.WriteLine(quotient); // 5
}</code></pre>

                <h2>Method Overloading</h2>
                <pre><code>public int Add(int a, int b)
{
    return a + b;
}

public double Add(double a, double b)
{
    return a + b;
}

public int Add(int a, int b, int c)
{
    return a + b + c;
}</code></pre>

                <div class="card bg-info bg-opacity-10 mb-4">
                    <div class="card-body">
                        <h5 class="card-title"><i class="fas fa-key me-2"></i>Key Takeaway</h5>
                        <p>Methods should do one thing and do it well. Use meaningful names and keep them focused.</p>
                    </div>
